Output charge and kinetic-energy density for the LCAO SCAN functional.

The Libxc correction retains local exchange-correlation energy and derivatives
at finite density when the density gradient vanishes. This applies to LCAO as
well as PW. The old LCAO cubes and scalar references preceded that correction:
with the old SCF settings the Fermi energy changes from 0.644033 to 0.644022 Ry,
which fails the existing cube comparison on both CPU and GPU.

Set scf_thr to 1e-10 and write 12-digit cube fields to resolve the output at the
existing pointwise limits: 1e-6 for charge and 1e-8 for kinetic-energy density.
The 100-step SCF budget, structure, orbital basis, cutoff, mixing and comparison
tolerances are unchanged. The reference comes from a CPU calculation at the
independently tighter scf_thr=1e-12. Tightening 1e-10 to 1e-12 changes the total
energy by less than 4e-13 eV, charge by 1.4e-12 and kinetic-energy density by
5.1e-12 over all 3375 grid points.

Cross-checks use GNU 12.3, OpenMPI 5.0.10 and one OpenMP/BLAS thread, with
Libxc 5.1.7 (the CI version) and 7.0.0. Explicit CPU/genelpa and GPU/cuSOLVER
runs at both one and two MPI ranks pass every original scalar and cube check.
The GPU checks use CUDA 13.1 and an RTX 3090; INPUT.info and the running log
confirm the selected device and eigensolver. No reference-comparison threshold
is relaxed. The preserved totaltimeref is not a numerical acceptance criterion.
